<title>UK: ICI to sell ICI Australia stake as part of Unilever deal.</title>
<headline>ICI to sell ICI Australia stake as part of Unilever deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch food to consumer products group Unilever Plc/NV said on Wednesday it agreed to sell its international speciality chemicals businesses to Imperial Chemical Industries Plc for $8.0 billion in cash.</p>
<p>Unilever said the sale would result in an exceptional gain, before tax and expenses, of more than $5.0 billion.</p>
<p>ICI said it planned to sell its 62.4 percent stake in ICI Australia as part of a plan to raise three billion stg over three years.</p>
</text>
